{'symbol': 'LMT', 'date': '2022-07-11 18:57:00', 'title': 'NASA RELEASES FIRST NEAR INFRARED CAMERA SCIENTIFIC IMAGE TAKEN BY JAMES WEBB SPACE TELESCOPE', 'text': "A LOCKHEED MARTIN-BUILT INSTRUMENT GIVES US A CLOSER LOOK AT THE UNIVERSE'S ORIGINS DENVER , JULY 11, 2022 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- TODAY AT A WHITE HOUSE PRESS EVENT, NASA RELEASED THE FIRST IMAGE OF SOME OF THE EARLIEST LIGHT IN OUR UNIVERSE, TAKEN WITH AN INSTRUMENT THAT LOCKHEED MARTIN (NYSE: LMT) DESIGNED AND BUILT. THE DEBUT PHOTO FROM THE JAMES WEBB SPACE TELESCOPE'S NEAR INFRARED CAMERA (NIRCAM) IS THE FIRST FROM ONE OF THE MOST SENSITIVE INFRARED CAMERAS EVER BUILT TO OBSERVE THE UNIVERSE."}